INT. BOMBED CATHEDRAL BELL TOWER - DAWN

Stone stairs spiral up into smoke. A great bronze bell hangs cracked. Slit windows. Dust falls like snow.

SGT. IMRE HALASZ, 40s, grey in his beard, crouches at a slit window. Rifle braced.

CPL. TEODORO BASCO, 20s, wiry, kneels beside a field radio. Headset crooked.

PVT. LI WEI, 19, round glasses taped at the hinge, sits against the wall. Hugging his helmet.

He stares at nothing.

LT. AGNES FARQUHAR, 30s, mud to the knees, climbs into the room. Pistol out. Breathing hard.

She drops beside the sergeant.

FARQUHAR
Report.

HALASZ
Two tanks at the bridge. Infantry behind them.

BASCO
Command says hold.

FARQUHAR
Hold what?

BASCO
The tower, ma'am.

FARQUHAR
We're in the tower.

BASCO
That's what I told them.

HALASZ
They've seen us. Light on the bell.

He points. A glint on the bronze.

FARQUHAR
Cover it.

LI
With what?

FARQUHAR
Your jacket.

He doesn't move.

HALASZ
Li.

LI
Yes, Sergeant.

HALASZ
Jacket.

He peels it off. Climbs the bell frame. Drapes it over the metal. Hands shaking.

A distant WHUMP.

BASCO
Incoming!

All four drop.

The wall SHUDDERS. Plaster rains.

FARQUHAR
Where?

HALASZ
Short. Nave.

BASCO
Sergeant, they're ranging us.

LI
They're ranging us. They're ranging us.

FARQUHAR
Private!

LI
I'm fine.

HALASZ
He's not fine.

FARQUHAR
Nobody's fine. Basco, get me the battery.

BASCO
Radio's dead on the artillery net.

FARQUHAR
Then use the infantry net.

BASCO
They don't answer.

HALASZ
Because they're running.

He turns back to the slit.

HALASZ (CONT'D)
Infantry's on the bridge. Fifty metres.

FARQUHAR
Count?

HALASZ
Thirty. Forty.

LI
We have nine magazines.

BASCO
Eight. I gave one to the medic.

LI
The medic's dead.

Silence. Basco looks at him. Then away.

Another WHUMP. Closer.

The bell RINGS, one flat note. Dust pours from the vault.

FARQUHAR
Down. Everyone down!

She grabs Li by the collar. Hauls him flat.

He grips her sleeve.

LI
Lieutenant, I can't.

FARQUHAR
You can.

LI
I can't.

HALASZ
Li. Look at me.

He does.

HALASZ (CONT'D)
Forty men on that bridge. Four of us up here. You know what that makes us?

LI
Dead.

HALASZ
Inconvenient.

A breath. Something almost like a laugh.

Basco slams the radio.

BASCO
Got them! Got somebody!

FARQUHAR
Who?

BASCO
Don't know. Sounds like cavalry.

HALASZ
We don't have cavalry.

BASCO
Then it's somebody's cousin.

The third shell lands. Direct hit on the stair below. The floor LURCHES.

They scramble. Rifles up. Faces white with plaster.

FARQUHAR
Positions.

He crawls to the slit. She takes the east window. Basco kneels, radio in one fist, rifle in the other.

Li lifts his rifle. Steadies it on the sill.

LI
Sergeant?

HALASZ
Yes?

LI
When it starts, don't let me stop.

HALASZ
I won't.

The bell hums. Beyond it, boots on the bridge.

HALASZ (CONT'D)
Wait for it.
